---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="ContinuityOS — durable local memory for agent workflows" description="Public source project for durable local memory and governance-oriented agent workflows.">
  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <div class="kicker">Public source · local-first</div>
      <h1>ContinuityOS</h1>
      <p>ContinuityOS is presented here as a public source project for durable local memory and governance-oriented agent workflows.</p>
      <p class="boundary"><strong>Evidence boundary:</strong> structured memory and provenance can reduce retrieval ambiguity; they do not eliminate model errors.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a href="https://github.com/bitmaster162/continuityos" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="button">Install from public GitHub source</a>
        <a href="/agent-authority-audit" class="button secondary">Audit methodology</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container content">
    <h2>What it is for</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article><h3>Durable local records</h3><p>Keep structured facts, rules, notes and provenance in a local store that can be inspected outside one model session.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Retrieval with provenance</h3><p>Use structured namespaces and retrieval signals to make the source of recalled context easier to inspect and challenge.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Governance-oriented workflows</h3><p>Separate remembered content from authority to act. Memory is context; it is not permission, proof of correctness, or a safety guarantee.</p></article>
    </div>

    <div class="status">
      <h2>Public-install status</h2>
      <p>For this public site, the independently verified installation path is the public GitHub source. A <code>pip install continuityos</code> claim is intentionally not advertised until the public package/release and a clean installation are independently verified.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .hero-section{padding:64px 0 34px}.hero-inner{text-align:center;max-width:860px}.kicker{color:var(--gold);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:900;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}.hero-inner h1{font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,3.6rem);margin:8px 0 14px}.hero-inner>p{color:var(--muted);font-family:'Lora',serif;font-size:1.05rem}.boundary{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:14px 16px}.boundary strong{color:var(--gold)}.actions{display:flex;gap:12px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:22px}.button{padding:11px 18px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong);font-weight:800}.button.secondary{color:var(--muted)}.content{max-width:980px;padding-block:20px 50px}.content h2{font-family:'Playfair Display',serif}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px}.grid article,.status{background:var(--paper-soft);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:20px}.grid h3{margin:0 0 8px}.grid p,.status p{margin:0;color:var(--muted)}.status{margin-top:22px}.status code{color:var(--gold)}@media(max-width:820px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  </style>
</Layout>
